  the restriction exemption program  as soon as it is safe to do so  okay thank you premier rick do you have  a follow-up today  yes uh i do it's it's cobit-related uh  and it's related to the convoy uh the  trucker convoy uh which you've talked  about before now we all know what the  stated purpose of the convoy is so i'm  not going to ask you  what you've already expressed about your  view of the convoy  but  do you see  this protest as also having  uh a broader and deeper message to  the federal government to canadia to all  canadian politicians  and to other decision makers  that this sort of grassroots  uh cross-country  convoy is happening is there some  message that you think political figures  and other  perhaps non-elected decision makers  should take seriously from watching this  well first rick i think it's important  to say that we should all be grateful  for truckers  they keep our  grocery store shelves stocked day in and  day out they have uh while a lot of  people were sheltering at home over much  of the past two years they were out  there on the roads in good weather and  bad um keeping us and our whole society  and economy rolling so thank you to the  truckers and uh i  i i think it's important to to to  acknowledge that secondly um rick  everybody has the right uh for  democratic and peaceful protest in our  country  and we should be respectful of that  uh i agree with those who are protesting  the  uh i think pointless quarantine rule  being applied to cross-border truckers  that's why i'm going to washington dc  today  to raise this with top american leaders  and i do hope that those organizing the  convoy do everything they can to make  sure that it's safe  uh i hope that they disassociate  themselves with anybody  in the convoy who might have extreme or  hateful views but i acknowledge that you  know in any big social movement there  are going to be some people with fringe  views  uh you know whenever the ndp shows up at  some of those uh so-